_site/
.sass-cache/
.jekyll-metadata
# Python bytecode from analysis scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Spent one-off migrations. update-towns-format.py rewrote nny-toponyms.html
# from one TOWNS data shape to another on 2026-03-22; it is not idempotent —
# a second run would double-wrap the entries it already converted.
_resources/update-towns-format.py

# Obsidian vault config — this repo is opened as a vault for writing posts.
# Workspace layout, plugin state and cache; none of it belongs on the site.
.obsidian/

# Symlink to the private sessions repo — see backlog/site.md there.
# This repo is PUBLIC; an internal backlog must not be committed to it.
BACKLOG.md

# Post drafts. This repo is PUBLIC, and _ideas/ is otherwise tracked, so a draft
# committed here is published on github.com even though Jekyll never builds it —
# working notes, inferences about intent, and TODO comments addressed to me,
# under my own name, attached to a post I may never run. Same reasoning as
# BACKLOG.md above: the pattern is the risk, not any one file's content.
#
# TWO rules, because a name-based rule is silently inert the moment someone
# names a file differently. `drafts/` is the safe drawer: anything put there is
# ignored by construction, no naming discipline required.
_ideas/*-draft.md
_ideas/drafts/
